commit 0fb66015bf10befec1d074a4471513bca92d572d
Author: Victor Gutierrez Calderon <victor@entire.io>
Date:   Fri Aug 14 10:21:58 2026 +0200

    fix: one answer to "which agents are available" across the agent surface

    Addresses the trail findings on #1930.

    - --external's help text and the externalOnly variable described the old
      "instead of" semantics; the flag has been a superset since 30e08df9e.
      Renamed to includeExternal and reworded to "Also list ...".
    - External entries in the superset listing rendered identically to
      built-ins. They are arbitrary executables resolved from $PATH, not code
      shipped in this binary, so they now carry an (external) suffix.
    - printAgentError contradicted `agent list`: it advertised test-only
      agents (vogon), omitted external plugins with no hint they exist, and
      always printed `Usage: entire enable --agent` even when reached from
      `entire agent add`. It now filters test-only agents, points at
      `entire agent list --external` (the error path deliberately does not
      pay for a $PATH scan), and takes the caller's usage line.
    - agent.ListResolved is the new single home for the test-only filter,
      shared by StringList, runAgentList, and printAgentError. It returns
      name+agent pairs because an external plugin's self-reported Name() is
      not validated against the registry key derived from its binary, and the
      registry key is the identity users type and agent.Get accepts.
      GetAgentsWithHooksInstalled stays on the unfiltered list on purpose:
      e2e installs vogon hooks and must keep seeing them.
    - SnapshotForTesting moved to registry_testing.go so the testing-only
      intent is legible at the call site, and its doc no longer implies
      safety against concurrent writers — restore replaces the whole map, so
      a Register landing mid-window is discarded.

    Verified: mise run fmt, golangci-lint 2.11.3 (0 issues), mise run test:ci
    (unit + integration + vogon 60/60 + roger-roger external canary 4/4).

